# Aligning Table Captions Left in LaTeX (Without caption Package)

Here are several methods to left-align table captions without using the `caption` package:

## Method 1: Using \captionsetup with floatrow

```latex
\usepackage{floatrow}
\floatsetup[table]{capposition=top}
\floatsetup{captionskip=10pt}
\floatsetup{justification=raggedright}
```

## Method 2: Redefining \@makecaption

Add this to your preamble:

```latex
\makeatletter
\long\def\@makecaption#1#2{%
  \vskip\abovecaptionskip
  \sbox\@tempboxa{#1: #2}%
  \ifdim \wd\@tempboxa >\hsize
    \raggedright #1: #2\par
  \else
    \raggedright #1: #2\par
  \fi
  \vskip\belowcaptionskip}
\makeatother
```

## Method 3: Simple Manual Approach

```latex
\begin{table}[h]
\begin{flushleft}
\caption{Your caption text here}
\end{flushleft}
\centering
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
A & B \\
\hline
1 & 2 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
```

## Method 4: Using a minipage

```latex
\begin{table}[h]
\begin{minipage}{\textwidth}
\raggedright
\caption{Your left-aligned caption}
\centering
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
A & B \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}
\end{table}
```

**Method 2** gives you the most control and affects all captions globally, while **Method 3** is quickest for a single table.

